# 基础词 Unit03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit03核心词汇

{{alone}}{/əˈləʊn/}{{adj. 独自的；adv. 独自地}}{{She lives alone in a small apartment.}}
{{along}}{/əˈlɒŋ/}{{prep. 沿着；adv. 一起}}{{We walked along the river bank.}}
{{alongside}}{/əˌlɒŋˈsaɪd/}{{prep. 在…旁边；与…一起}}{{The boat was anchored alongside the pier.}}
{{alphabet}}{/ˈælfəbet/}{{n. 字母表}}{{The English alphabet has 26 letters.}}
{{alter}}{/ˈɔːltər/}{{v. 改变；修改}}{{They decided to alter the original plan.}}
{{alternative}}{/ɔːlˈtɜːrnətɪv/}{{n. 替代选择；adj. 可替代的}}{{We need to find an alternative solution.}}
{{although}}{/ɔːlˈðəʊ/}{{conj. 虽然；尽管}}{{Although it was raining, we still went out.}}
{{altogether}}{/ˌɔːltəˈɡeðər/}{{adv. 完全地；总共}}{{The project was altogether successful.}}
{{aluminum}}{/əˈluːmɪnəm/}{{n. 铝}}{{Aluminum is widely used in manufacturing.}}
{{always}}{/ˈɔːlweɪz/}{{adv. 总是；一直}}{{She always arrives on time for meetings.}}
{{amateur}}{/ˈæmətər/}{{n. 业余爱好者；adj. 业余的}}{{He is an amateur photographer who takes beautiful pictures.}}
{{amaze}}{/əˈmeɪz/}{{v. 使惊奇；使惊叹}}{{The magic show amazed the audience.}}
{{ambassador}}{/æmˈbæsədər/}{{n. 大使；代表}}{{He served as the ambassador to France.}}
{{ambition}}{/æmˈbɪʃn/}{{n. 雄心；抱负}}{{Her ambition is to become a successful lawyer.}}
{{ambitious}}{/æmˈbɪʃəs/}{{adj. 有雄心的；野心勃勃的}}{{He is an ambitious young man with big dreams.}}
{{amend}}{/əˈmend/}{{v. 修正；改进}}{{The committee voted to amend the constitution.}}
{{among}}{/əˈmʌŋ/}{{prep. 在…之中}}{{She is among the top students in her class.}}
{{amount}}{/əˈmaʊnt/}{{n. 数量；总额}}{{A large amount of money was spent on the project.}}
{{amuse}}{/əˈmjuːz/}{{v. 逗乐；给…提供娱乐}}{{The comedian amused the crowd with his jokes.}}
{{analyze}}{/ˈænəlaɪz/}{{v. 分析；解析}}{{Scientists analyzed the data carefully.}}
{{ancestor}}{/ˈænsestər/}{{n. 祖先；祖宗}}{{Our ancestors lived in this village for centuries.}}
{{ancient}}{/ˈeɪnʃənt/}{{adj. 古代的；古老的}}{{The ancient ruins attract tourists from all over the world.}}
{{anger}}{/ˈæŋɡər/}{{n. 愤怒；v. 使发怒}}{{He tried to控制his anger during the argument.}}
{{angle}}{/ˈæŋɡl/}{{n. 角度；观点}}{{Let's look at the problem from a different angle.}}
{{angry}}{/ˈæŋɡri/}{{adj. 生气的；愤怒的}}{{She was angry about the unfair treatment.}}
{{animal}}{/ˈænɪml/}{{n. 动物}}{{Many endangered animals need our protection.}}
{{announce}}{/əˈnaʊns/}{{v. 宣布；通知}}{{The company announced a new product launch.}}
{{annoy}}{/əˈnɔɪ/}{{v. 使烦恼；使恼怒}}{{Loud noises annoy the neighbors.}}
{{annual}}{/ˈænjuəl/}{{adj. 每年的；n. 年刊}}{{The company holds an annual meeting in December.}}
{{anonymous}}{/əˈnɒnɪməs/}{{adj. 匿名的}}{{The donation was made by an anonymous donor.}}
{{another}}{/əˈnʌðər/}}{{adj. 另一个的；pron. 另一个}}{{Would you like another cup of tea?}}
{{answer}}{/ˈɑːnsər/}{{n. 回答；v. 回答}}{{She gave a quick answer to the question.}}
{{anticipate}}{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}{{v. 预期；期望}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in sales.}}
{{anxiety}}{/æŋˈzaɪəti/}{{n. 焦虑；不安}}{{Exam anxiety is common among students.}}
{{anxious}}{/ˈæŋkʃəs/}{{adj. 焦虑的；渴望的}}{{She felt anxious about the interview.}}
{{any}}{/ˈeni/}{{adj. 任何的；pron. 任何一个}}{{Do you have any questions for me?}}
{{apart}}{/əˈpɑːrt/}{{adv. 分开地；相距}}{{The two cities are 100 miles apart.}}
{{apartment}}{/əˈpɑːrtmənt/}{{n. 公寓}}{{They rent a small apartment in the city center.}}
{{apologize}}{/əˈpɒlədʒaɪz/}{{v. 道歉}}{{He apologized for being late to the meeting.}}
{{apparent}}{/əˈpærənt/}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的}}{{The solution was apparent to everyone in the room.}}
